Description: Nodes for multivariate analysis in a trama graph: principal
    component analysis with scree, biplot and correlation circle; factor
    analysis by maximum likelihood or principal axis, with orthogonal
    (varimax, quartimax, equamax) and oblique (promax, oblimin) rotations;
    linear and quadratic discriminant analysis with exact leave-one-out
    predictions; logistic regression (binary and multinomial) as a
    classifier; jackknife bias, standard errors and pseudovalues for
    component, factor,
    discriminant and logistic statistics; and the diagnostics that come
    first (KMO, Bartlett's sphericity, Horn's parallel analysis, Box's M);
    distance matrices (Euclidean, Mahalanobis D2, Gower), hierarchical
    clustering with cophenetic correlation, k-means and Tocher's
    optimization method; and one-way MANOVA with optional blocks.
    Ships example data with known structure. Builds on trama.data for
    tables, trama.view for plots and trama.models, whose model contract
    the classifiers implement (prediction, confusion and ROC are its nodes).
